  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a4100.html",
  "prefLabel": "Env-A 4103.24 General purpose adhesive remover",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 4103.24 “General purpose adhesive remover” means a product designed or labeled to remove cyanoacrylate adhesives as well as non-reactive adhesives or residue from a variety of substrates. The term includes, but is not limited to, products that remove thermoplastic adhesives, pressure sensitive adhesives, dextrine or starch-based adhesives, casein glues, and rubber or latex-based adhesives, as well as products that remove stickers, decals, stencils, or similar materials. The term does not include floor or wall covering adhesive remover.\n\nSource. #10527, eff 2-26-14; ss by #13969, eff 5-21-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a4100.html"
